# Analysis Rules (No Suppositions)

- When the user asks for an “analysis”, never base it on old assumptions or previous document versions.
- Always run fresh, read-only checks against the current main repo (e.g., `rg`/search, file existence, line counts) and cite the evidence in the response.
- If required data cannot be gathered, explicitly say what is missing and ask permission/scope for additional verification.

